<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>SquiFlow</title>
    <style>
        :root { font-family: Inter, system-ui, sans-serif; color-scheme: light dark; }
        body { margin: 0; }
        main { max-width: 920px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 48px 24px; }
        .eyebrow { opacity: .65; font-size: .82rem; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; }
        .panel { border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 18%, transparent); border-radius: 10px; padding: 24px; margin-top: 28px; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <main>
        <div class="eyebrow">Tenant Web · Phase 0</div>
        <h1>SquiFlow host foundation</h1>
        <p>This surface is intentionally not a fake business dashboard. Phase 0 proves executable and module boundaries; real journeys arrive in their owning slices.</p>
        <div class="panel">
            <strong>Customers module</strong>
            <p>The same host-neutral module semantics used by Workstation and Core API are available to this Web host without importing Avalonia or server persistence code.</p>
        </div>
    </main>
</body>
</html>
